.TH WMNOTIFYCTL 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmnotifyctl \- control wmnotify
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmnotifyctl
.I command
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "dnd " [ on | off | toggle | status ]
Do not disturb: nothing pops up except critical notifications.
.TP
.BI mute " APP"
Stop pop-ups from an application (names are case-insensitive, no spaces or commas).
.TP
.BI unmute " APP"
Undo \fBmute\fR.
.TP
.B muted
List muted applications.
.TP
.BR history " [" COUNT ]
Recent notifications, including hidden ones.
.TP
.B clear\-history
Forget them.
.TP
.B test
Show a test notification.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Settings are stored with \fBwmsettings\fR and take effect on the next notification.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmnotify (1),
.BR wmsettings (1)
